{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>Such is the place of him who knows not El</b> — it is transposed: 'such is the place of him who knows not El' comes first, then what is with it. Likewise it is: 'such is the place of him who knows not El' is transposed."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is itself a compressed metatextual note about word order; both lines appear to repeat the same claim about transposition (עול = עיתוק/היפוך). The phrasing is elliptical and possibly corrupt; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:00.333119844Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}